reagent-name-gasoil = Gas-oil
reagent-desc-gasoil = Heavy, suffocating fumes of crude oil. The gas is colorless with a barely perceptible oily sheen, has a characteristic pungent smell of hydrocarbons. It is flammable, when burning. At high concentrations, it is toxic and causes suffocation by displacing oxygen.
reagent-name-naphtha = Naphtha
reagent-desc-naphtha = A highly flammable mixture of liquid hydrocarbons. Clear, with a sharp petroleum-like odor. Used as a solvent, fuel, or component for synthesizing other substances. Inhalation causes dizziness and nausea.
